# Corpus/External is committed, not ignored: every shader in it carries an
# explicit permissive licence and the header naming its author, its page and
# that licence, so a clone has the corpus the tables are measured over without
# asking anything of the network. See Corpus/README.md.

# What shadertoy-scan leaves behind: a header per shader that converted, and
# the registration naming the ones that then compiled. A measurement of this
# compiler and these flags, so it belongs to a build directory and not here.
/scan
